            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of thyrocalcitonin on the pain sensitivity in animals].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With a single parenteral introduction of thyrocalcitonin (TCT) the algesthesia of soft tissues (tall skin, paw) is moderately increasing, while the algesic action of morphine and promedol against the background of TCT-gets weaker. And contrarywise algesthesia of hard tissues of the tooth becomes significantly lower under the effect of TCT and this continues for a long time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
